# scyBorg Triple License

This work is licensed under the **scyBorg triple copyleft**:

## 1. AGPL-3.0-or-later — Code

All code, templates, build scripts, and infrastructure configuration.

Full text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html

## 2. ORC — Methodology & Game Mechanics

All methodology patterns, frameworks, capability definitions, coordination
protocols, and operational procedures. The ORC license applies to the
guerillaGorilla methodology the same way it applies to game mechanics:
the patterns are open, reusable, and derivative works must remain open.

Full text: https://paizo.com/community/blog/v5748dyo6sico

## 3. CC-BY-SA 4.0 — Content & Documentation

All written content, analysis, documentation, and site pages.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

---

## Why Three Licenses

Each license covers a different layer of the work:

| Layer | License | What it covers |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Code** | AGPL-3.0-or-later | Zola templates, build crates, litho-core, infrastructure |
| **Methodology** | ORC | fEAR/preSCENT/STRIDe framework, pursuit predation, amicusContra, dispersal pattern |
| **Content** | CC-BY-SA 4.0 | Written pages, analysis, case studies, documentation |

The scyBorg triple ensures that every layer of the work remains open.
If you use the code, your code must be open (AGPL).
If you use the methodology, your methodology must be open (ORC).
If you use the content, your content must be attributed and shared alike (CC-BY-SA).

